    "turn_text": "Well, it helps if you're budget neutral and then you simply put that cap on the various programs or the titles of the bill. There's 12 of them. And you don't want to be skipping titles and having pay fors in other sections of the bill. But it does force some very tough policy decisions. We don't want to be in the position of going way over budget. Several commodities. I received a lot of help in the omnibus bill that was sometime back. I think we can get a good bill under the current budget. It's just that we have to get our work done and make sure that with regards to the conference committee, don't forget that what was it. We could go We had 56 people taking part. I think that's a little wild and woolly, but at any rate we have nine confries in the Senate and 47 in the House. So right now we have what we call the Fab Four and that's Colin Pearson from Minnesota and Deb Sabenoff from Michigan, myself from Kansas and obviously Mike from Texas.",
