    "turn_idx": 27,
    "turn_text": "Well, I would say that tomorrow never would proceed to the ground if it didn't take me to have a crop and we think that we can get an agreement. It's going to take a lot of hard work because we have some differences of opinion that are pretty serious with regards to policy. That has to be worked out. If we cannot, you have in December really, but you're talking about a lame duck session of Congress, that That could be a possibility. And then if you run out of rope, you always have an extension possibility. Unfortunately, that happened in the last Farm Bill and it went from year to year to year. Farmers don't want that. I have been saying over and over and over again that farmers deserve predictability and certainty and that that issue is paramount over any other. So I hope if we can adhere to that, we can get it done.",
